**Root cause of the check timeout (all measured live):** this host's WSL resolver stalls ~10s on every AAAA query while A-only lookups answer in 3-13ms. gh is a static Go binary - `GODEBUG=netdns=cgo` and `RES_OPTIONS` are no-ops on it - and Go resolves A+AAAA in parallel, so every one of the suite's 163 gh calls paid the stall. That is the entire 25-minute runtime; one pinned call drops 11.7s -> 0.199s.

**Repair 2 (tests/receipt-gates.sh only):** a preamble that resolves both GitHub hostnames A-only and re-execs the suite inside `unshare -rm` with a namespace-private /etc/hosts pin. No system file touched, addresses re-resolved per run, hosts without unprivileged namespaces fall through unpinned with a loud note. No helper byte and no gate byte touched - verified by regenerating the patch's original test file and diffing (only preamble + Gate 7 + final PASS line differ).

**Verification, live this session:** suite 25min -> 1m15.3s, exit 0, `PASS: receipt gates 0-7`; budget-check green at 196/200 SLOC; `gh repo list | grep jrit-loop-scratch` empty (the sweep even deleted the repo ringer's SIGKILLed check leaked); check structural steps 1,3,5,7,8 replicated and green; NOTES contract held, zero em dashes.

